  "name": "positional-member-fixability",
  "description": "A dead constant whose deletion changes the value of a live constant of its group is a positional member: a later specification repeats its expression list, or a later expression list uses iota. A finding about one carries manual fixability and a component that removes no line, under the code its references select, and so does a finding about a dead declaration only such a member names. A dead constant before such a held constant in its group is held as well, because the held constant's value depends on it, and so is a dead name of a specification that also declares a live name, which a later specification repeats. A dead name of a specification that writes no expression list, beside a live name of the same specification, is positional as well, because deleting it leaves fewer names than the list the specification repeats has expressions. A dead constant whose deletion changes no live value carries its code's own fixability, and shares a component with each dead constant whose value its deletion changes, so a wholly dead group deletes whole. A specification that writes no expression list references the type the repeated list names, so an enumerated type a live member repeats stays live.",
